.KEY x
.BRA {
.KET }
;
; Multi-block writes to the card, for comparison on the host afterwards.
;
; Upstream 6042b4a8ea found that SDHOST on Pi 1-3 can drop the last block of
; a write when CMD12 follows the DMA too closely, and still report success.
; Nothing on this side can see that, so the copies are read back off the
; image after shutdown and compared with the originals byte for byte:
;
;   mcopy -i out/aros/sd.img@@1M ::sdwrite/<name> - | cmp - <original>
;
; Three sizes: two multi-block writes, one of them not a multiple of 512, and
; one small file.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[sdwrite] start"
MakeDir SYS:sdwrite
Copy LIBS:lzma.library SYS:sdwrite/lzma.library >DEBUG:
Copy LIBS:png.library SYS:sdwrite/png.library >DEBUG:
Copy C:Copy SYS:sdwrite/Copy >DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[sdwrite] done"
